@YYY A:
This is a little hard to answer without knowing what the doctor prescribed. I would be very careful with your husband's health (especially if he is taking any prescription medications). There are a lot of possible side effects with Dox-cyclin.
One possibility is that your doctor may not be aware of the side-effects of this medication. If he has not ordered a full panel of lab tests to ensure that he does not have an infection, then he might not know that the antibiotics can cause an overgrowth of bacteria in the blood. In this case, it would not hurt to get the full results from the lab, even if it means taking a few extra days off of work. Then, if your physician is concerned about your health, he should ask you to come back in two weeks with a complete blood count, stool test for parasites, etc. and then start the treatment.

