The spot could very well be a fungus.
However, it may be nothing but a small fungal growth, and there is no need to see a urologist. There is only a need for you to wash the area with an antibacterial soap and use a topical antifungal cream. The cream should be applied to the spot in the morning and evening, alternating with a daily application of the antibacterial solution. Also, do not use the cream or antibacterial solutions for a long time as they can become infected with bacteria and cause secondary infection. Good luck.}}
